  "conclusions": [
    "Do not adopt ten block-local clusters blindly: some groups lose much of the globallyshared conservative target pool or cannot reach all their ownobserver footprints even in terrain-free coverage. Per-group details quantify this without claiming full local A* proof.",
    "Local grouping can reduce duplicate pursuit and long global scout tours only if target ownership/claims and actual bounded routes are solved. The present direct-tour figures are lower bounds, not measured or collision-aware tour costs.",
    "All-nine stable6 geometry is conservative over original observerbody positions. It is not a live target census or an upper bound on targets that may wander in; no conclusion establishes or denies actual localpoolcapacity.",
    "The fractional max-min calculation allows ideal divisible targetrefresh capacity and ignores travel/killtime/death/respawn overhead; it exposes shared-ID allocation bottlenecks only under the frozen conditional model. It is not a deterministic60second guarantee.",
    "The same physical spawn must not be credited independently to multiple local pools. Global123 is not123 per fighter. Expected positive hits do not prove18launched/min; actual formal25 almost all launches hit, so unmodeledmisses cannot be assumed to create safe slack.",
    "Under original ordinary fresh growth, fullglobal100 idealL5=186.46positive/min is only a small conditionalmargin near180launch/min and L10/L15 drop151.47/130.47. Real level/effectiveDC were not fully logged and cannot be inferred solely from formal damage; two-hour demand cannot be frozen atL1.",
    "First resolve the observed duplicate-chase gap without weakening activity gates. If a later scene proposal is authorized, keep first10 and verify each laterprefix has exclusive or explicitlyshared targetallocation, original4000node local routes, finite scoutcost, realstable6witnesses and adequate conditional bands; this inventory does not certify a feasible100localpoollayout."
  ],
